cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use XRDLab in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "XRDLab: open-source X-ray diffraction (XRD) and high-resolution XRD analysis for epitaxial thin films"
abstract: >-
  XRDLab is a free, open-source desktop application for analysing X-ray
  diffraction data from thin films and producing publication-quality figures.
  It reads Panalytical .xrdml files (2θ-ω scans, ω rocking curves, φ scans and
  reciprocal-space maps) and provides stacked waterfall plots, phase
  identification, doublet-aware peak widths (FWHM), rocking-curve analysis with
  threading-dislocation density and mosaic tilt/twist, reciprocal-space-map
  strain and relaxation, thickness from Pendellösung (Laue) fringes,
  Williamson–Hall analysis, and vector (PDF/EPS/SVG) export.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Rqsh-c0des
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Rqsh-c0des/xrdlab"
url: "https://rqsh-c0des.github.io/xrdlab/"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-29"
keywords:
